# JARVIS — Windsurf rules

Canonical source: AGENTS.md / CONVENTIONS.md. These are hard constraints.

ENTRY POINTS
- main.py is THE entry point: `python main.py` (HUD dashboard), `python main.py --terminal` (text).
  Flow: main.py -> core/orchestrator.py -> core/reasoning_core.py -> core/agentic_core.py -> tools/*.
- Never wire anything to jarvis_main.py or agent_fabric.py (deprecated). gui.py = dashboard alias.

PLUGGABLE BRAIN (free, local-first)
- No API key required. Without ANTHROPIC_API_KEY -> local Ollama (llm_router.local_mode()), model env
  OLLAMA_MODEL (default llama3.1:8b), host env OLLAMA_HOST; vision env OLLAMA_VISION_MODEL (default
  llava:7b). With a key, Claude is used/preferred. main.py::_startup_check() boots on ANY reachable
  brain and hard-fails only when none exists.
- Core runtime is PURE STANDARD LIBRARY. Optional packages go behind `try/except ImportError` and
  degrade honestly - never crash, never fake success.

BRAIN SETUP UI
- Both dashboards (HUD ui/hud.html at /, classic ui/dashboard.html at /classic) have a gear SETUP panel ->
  GET /api/brains + POST /api/brain {"name","model"} + POST /api/brain/test {"name"} (test WITHOUT switching;
  LLMClient.test_profile) in channels/web_server.py; persists to config/settings.json (non-secret only).
  The API NEVER accepts or returns raw keys - only a key_present boolean + the env-var NAME. Keys live
  solely in .env (gitignored).

SAFETY GATES - DO NOT WEAKEN
- security.py, core/permission_gate.py, core/permission_manager.py, core/safety_guard.py.
- Deletion, overwrite, shell, installs, external comms, system changes, money/trading stay
  confirmation-gated; self-modification of PROTECTED_SOURCE stays blocked. pyautogui.FAILSAFE=True always.
- Never edit a gate to make a failing test pass - the gate wins; report the disagreement.

SECRETS
- Never commit/print/log/store keys. .env is gitignored. No secrets in code, config, memory, notes, tests.

CLICK_ELEMENT
- "click the submit button" -> VisionCore.locate (UIA tree -> two-pass vision -> single-pass) -> click_at;
  module path modules/gui_automation.py::click_element -> vision_engine.locate_element (% -> pixels).
  Grounding is best-effort - verify after clicking.

TESTS
- `python -m pytest tests/ -q --tb=no`. Known-failing baseline (upstream, NOT regressions; don't weaken
  gates to fix): tests/test_hardening.py (3) + tests/test_core.py::test_agentic_brain_chains_actions.
  Don't change llm_router.complexity_score() / classify_task().

PLATFORM
- Windows 10/11 target. SAPI voice, Task Scheduler, UI Automation, app control can't be tested on Linux -
  say so; never claim verified.
